==Old English==

===Etymology===
From an earlier form {{m|ang|hlāfweard}}, from {{m|ang|hlāf}} + {{m|ang|weard}}. Equivalent to {{m|en|loaf}} + {{m|en|ward}}. See also {{m|ang|hlǣfdīġe}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈl̥ɑːvord/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hlāford|m|hlāfordas}}

# [[lord]], master of servants
# male head of a household

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-m|hlāford}}

====Descendants====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|lhoaverd}}, {{l|enm|louerd}}, {{l|enm|lord}}
** Scots: {{l|sco|laird}}
** English: {{l|en|lord}}
* → Old Norse: {{l|non|lávarði}}

